mipi_rgb: ESPHome's mipi_rgb display component with three fixes and two additions for the Guition ESP32-S3-4848S040

Derived from ESPHome 2026.9.1 (https://github.com/esphome/esphome, tag 2026.9.1, commit
0b2b16e664ecfc0add37f3435db1c2140b8a687e; esphome/components/mipi_rgb last changed in fe3788ff4783).
Copyright the ESPHome authors. The C++ files are GPLv3 (LICENSE here); the Python files are MIT, as in ESPHome.

Changed (each marked "Facet" in the source):
- mipi_rgb.cpp: wait 120 ms after SWRESET and after SLPOUT before the next init command (the ST7701S datasheet
  times). Stock ESPHome sent the next block at once, so the panel dropped the first settings block (wrong blacks,
  lifted greys, flicker).
- mipi_rgb.cpp: the RGB bounce buffer is PANEL_BOUNCE_ROWS rows (a build flag, default 10 as stock).
- mipi_rgb.cpp/.h: VSYNC and frame-complete counters (IRAM callbacks) for /fw/info "lcd", and get_handle() for
  Facet's direct LVGL flush (board/rgb_flush.h).
- mipi_rgb.h: no loop() on the ESP32-S3. Stock ESPHome restarted the RGB DMA on every loop pass, which shifted
  frames (a red-tinted flicker); the ESP-IDF driver already restarts after a real underflow.

Everything else is ESPHome's file as released. Facet drops this copy when ESPHome carries these fixes.
